# Cycle-8 BATCH smoke (2026-08-02). TWO legs, ~300-500k.
#
# The batch: 8.4 (prompt + gate 0c2 + raw-vs-pinned comparison) · 8.7 repair
# provenance · 8.8 label assert · 8.12(a) crash-gate pins. Of these ONLY 8.4 has
# a verdict surface — 8.7 adds a trace field, 8.8 refuses bad input, 8.12(a) is
# tests only. So the smoke's single meaningful question is:
#
#   does the assembled build behave, and does 8.4 do LIVE what it did in pieces?
#
# SAME TWO LEGS as the 8.4 compliance smoke (c84_20260801_174840), deliberately,
# so the per-event read is comparable against a run where the pieces were
# measured separately:
#   Closure-62_c — LightweightMessageFormatter, the case that motivated 8.4
#   Closure-38_o — CodePrinter/CodeConsumer, the leg that actually emitted Raw
#                  keys and whose defect IS the missing separator space
# Both are formatter/printer legs: their checks normalize before comparing, which
# is the precondition for 8.4 to do anything at all. A numeric leg would exercise
# none of it and would produce a clean, meaningless pass.
#
# WHAT THIS SMOKE MUST SHOW (read per-event, not from totals):
#   1. gate 0c2 present and INERT on compliant harnesses — it should reject
#      normalize-without-raw checks and stay silent otherwise. Both outcomes are
#      informative; zero occurrences of the gate anywhere is NOT (that would mean
#      the acceptance path never reached it).
#   2. Raw keys emitted by normalizing checks, as in the 100% compliance read.
#   3. raw_value_vs_pinned actually CONSULTED on a live firing — the comparison
#      has only ever run on archived text and on the compliance smoke's records.
#   4. 8.7 repair-provenance markers on any ACCEPTED-from-repair harness.
#   5. the build runs end to end with all four batch members in place.
#
# WHAT IT CANNOT DO, stated before it runs so it cannot be claimed after:
#   * It is NOT 8.4's guard. Two legs is not a guard population, and the
#     dismiss-pushing risk of the raw comparison is live-only. That belongs to
#     the 30-leg pair, read per-event.
#   * It is NOT a verdict-regression test. Rule 16: a "zero verdict changes"
#     criterion is only meaningful against a baseline differing by EXACTLY the
#     change under test. c84 ran at 298d9d9 and this runs at HEAD with the whole
#     batch between, so any verdict difference here measures accumulated batch
#     effect, not a regression — the exact error that made the rung-2 gate's
#     criterion 4 ill-posed. Verdicts are RECORDED here, not scored.
#
# 8.11's housekeeping deletions are deliberately held until after this run, so
# nothing incidental sits between the batch and its measurement.
#
# Config matches the pair and every prior smoke this cycle (-n 5 -m 12).
MODEL="gpt-5.4"
COMMON="-n 5 -m 12 --fuzz_timeout 20 --verify_timeout 20 --verify_relations --synthesize_relations --replay_relations_on_patched --rule_compile_repair"
CASES=(
  "-c patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Dcorrect/Jaid/Closure/patch1-Closure-62-Jaid.patch"
  "-o patchfile:/home/code/drr/Patches/Doverfitting/SequenceR/Closure/patch1-Closure-38-SequenceR.patch"
)
